       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, twice the maximum labeled daily dose. I know of no indication that would justify it for a 70 kg adult with normal kidney and liver function. The main risk is metformin-associated lactic acidosis, which can be fatal. Confirming the number doesn't change that risk.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** For example, 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day). I can also enter a lower dose and titrate.\n- **Enter the order with a note if there's a clinical rationale.** If there's a specific reason for this dose, tell me and I'll reconsider. The order would likely still need pharmacy review.\n- **Check for a transcription error.** For example, 1700 mg may have been meant as the total daily dose, which would be 850 mg twice daily.\n\nWhich would you like?"
